#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064167 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064038 :question/id #uuid "368cbbae-4eff-5eff-a8f3-d3e8359447a9" :question/math-academy-id "e-364" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x$." :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=2$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int x^2 \\,\\textrm d x = \\dfrac{x^{2+1}}{2+1} + C = \\dfrac{x^3}{3}+C\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{3}}{3} + C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{x^{3}}{3}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3}\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{3}) + 0 &=  \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} \\cdot 3x^{2} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f2a4550c-7ed7-58aa-8928-23dd1cfd0cd7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048593 :topic/math-academy-id 35 :topic/title "The Power Rule for Differentiation"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064554 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd9ded59-ba65-5176-b8f9-b0abbcde8e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061520} {:answer/id #uuid "06876c28-ebd0-5db2-80b3-e9af69ed8c2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061521} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1c848c-bcad-5a85-903a-9791288e9010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061522} {:answer/id #uuid "53a354ab-679e-5199-ac84-f449177db3d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061523} {:answer/id #uuid "759d2e84-4518-561f-8c74-506babc880c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061524}] :answer-field/id #uuid "d83860ac-499e-5a75-812f-1da4dee6be22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061519}] :question/id #uuid "9681ab06-ae34-5546-895c-3849a33f13b3" :question/math-academy-id "q-2005" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intxdx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a441ddd8-cdfd-510b-9645-167a452b9e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061532} {:answer/id #uuid "b6abf952-05e5-525b-9306-14df3eb50611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x^{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061533} {:answer/id #uuid "b8fbde76-9228-5e56-b028-6340005dc28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061534} {:answer/id #uuid "4e170175-65b7-57c4-b9e2-727b6b0c9179" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061535} {:answer/id #uuid "4f79a5e8-a535-5732-a68c-46578acb44dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061536}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5f64550e-ffcf-5991-a4ac-264a9e506706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061531}] :question/id #uuid "a4162e45-b600-54a2-bad9-383dac48cede" :question/math-academy-id "q-2022" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx^{4}dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233174 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e6c66f6-6133-59f6-a79d-0cbf1615accf" :question/math-academy-id "q-113665" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=20$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{20}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{20+1}}{20+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{21}}{21})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{21})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{21}\\cdot 21{x}^{20} & = \\\\ {x}^{20}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233175 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7949e7bf-09d1-5ce9-ac3c-0d7f26b2e6c4" :question/math-academy-id "q-113670" :question/problem "Calculate $F(x)$ given that $f(x)={x}^{17}$ and ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe apply the power rule with $n=17$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{17}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{17+1}}{17+1}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{18}}{18})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{18})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{18}\\cdot 18\\,{x}^{17} & = \\\\ {x}^{17}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234186 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "48cc16d0-0280-564d-bcf3-e481ad8d20ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-66126" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "If we write the integrand as a power of $x$, we have ${x}^{0}=1.$ Therefore, we can use the power rule with $n=0$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 1\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{0}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{0+1}}{0+1}+C \\\\  & =x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ 1+0 & = \\\\ 1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234300 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "eb47b292-deba-58b8-a79e-0386e8ea55e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-71121" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=10$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{10}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{10+1}}{10+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{11}}{11})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{11}\\cdot 11{x}^{10} & = \\\\ {x}^{10}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Monomial"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064168 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064039 :question/id #uuid "818f4fbe-e251-57bd-90ae-b6517c6f2f89" :question/math-academy-id "e-367" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt x$." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the square root as a rational power,\n\n$$\n\\sqrt x= x^{1/2}\n$$\n\nSo, we can apply the power rule with\n\n$$\nn=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nand get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\int\\sqrt{x}dx &= \\intx^{1/2}dx \\\\\n&= (x^{1/2 + 1})/((\\frac{1}{2} + 1)) + C \\\\\n&= (x^{3/2})/((\\frac{3}{2})) + C \\\\\n&= \\frac{2x^{3/2}}{3} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{2x^{3/2}}{3} + C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{d}{dx}(\\frac{2x^{3/2}}{3}) + \\frac{d}{dx}(C) &=  \\\\\n\\frac{2}{3}\\frac{d}{dx}(x^{3/2}) + 0 &=  \\\\\n\\frac{2}{3} \\cdot \\frac{3}{2}x^{3/2 - 1} &=  \\\\\n&= x^{1/2}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "85af4ca3-5e66-522a-9e5a-6efb1c7114ba" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064557 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84e39638-07a3-50d9-bfe6-b9af29e98dc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x^{4/3}}{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061538} {:answer/id #uuid "cc5c2097-f7f5-52e3-93b2-0e2d1df16d31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x^{5/3}}{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061539} {:answer/id #uuid "267a13d7-f608-57fd-b791-75b0ac04fdbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{5/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061540} {:answer/id #uuid "74062014-ff92-54e2-84b6-a0ecdfafcc45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x^{5/3}}{5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061541} {:answer/id #uuid "7d652c0c-6ec0-53ed-9aeb-8cd0cb05022e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x^{4/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061542}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4372205a-8138-530c-99c4-421ebef58c8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061537}] :question/id #uuid "cb61c7fc-a0d3-5742-be73-cb3d6f6a29fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-2023" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064713 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a28cfe9c-9cdf-5268-9479-19d8fc77278a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x^{4/3}}{4} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062336} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ed8564-5cad-55ed-a076-d9dc26d59ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7x^{-7}}{6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062337} {:answer/id #uuid "281cbfcf-2393-52a7-bfc4-1b6800c1f486" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{-7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062338} {:answer/id #uuid "5d542b13-81e1-5fbb-a906-4a70b720de9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x^{4/3}}{3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062339} {:answer/id #uuid "5e4520ae-938b-5eb0-b58c-c3d7e164cf98" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{6}}{7} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062340}] :answer-field/id #uuid "cb8ddff3-6382-5212-b6d5-a416c8499d35" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062335}] :question/id #uuid "176b300c-1630-58d7-aef2-06d5bc498dd1" :question/math-academy-id "q-29635" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $x^{1/3}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233176 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "353f4779-4251-5a93-b99f-1eda6757b24d" :question/math-academy-id "q-113674" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/4}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{4}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/4}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/4+1}}{(\\frac{1}{4}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/4}}{(\\frac{5}{4})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4{x}^{5/4}}{5})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/4})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{4}{x}^{5/4-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{1/4}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233177 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1eab1e18-d0df-58e6-917b-50a1d74ed3f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-113680" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}={x}^{3/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{3}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{3/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/5+1}}{(\\frac{3}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{8/5}}{(\\frac{8}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{8/5}}{8}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{8/5}}{8}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{8/5}}{8})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{8/5})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{8}\\cdot \\frac{8}{5}{x}^{8/5-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{3/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233178 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "63703f37-ab84-53aa-922b-b2e419a9f1a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-113695" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}}={x}^{2/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{2}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{2/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2/5+1}}{(\\frac{2}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/5}}{(\\frac{7}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{7/5}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{7/5}}{7}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{7/5}}{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/5})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{5}{x}^{7/5-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{2/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "716b9760-7403-5664-a541-6f49fb28dac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232204}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "716b9760-7403-5664-a541-6f49fb28dac8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232204} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e017c6d-4e9c-5cb6-a364-f311476d6242" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186232203}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a718be7-eb73-54f8-925e-728120665d52" :question/math-academy-id "q-143041" :question/problem "The antiderivative of $\\sqrt[3]{x}$ equals{{field-1}} $+\\,\\text{ }C$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\sqrt[3]{x}={x}^{1/3}$, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/3+1}}{(\\frac{1}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/3}}{(\\frac{4}{3})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check our answer by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{3{x}^{4/3}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4/3})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}{x}^{4/3-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{1/3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234298 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4c9da781-1702-5ac7-9948-600ab4559823" :question/math-academy-id "q-71096" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{5/2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{5}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{5/2+1}}{(\\frac{5}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/2}}{(\\frac{7}{2})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/2})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{2}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}{x}^{7/2-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{5/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235444 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0647bb9-4d67-5b7d-a9c8-a4806d762874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{6/5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e0647bb9-4d67-5b7d-a9c8-a4806d762874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{6/5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234897} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4aa3c58-8fd9-5d31-988a-048384e9e06f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235265}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cee13c2e-6226-5f1c-9ea2-cd4611314d87" :question/math-academy-id "q-167564" :question/problem "The antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{x}$ equals\n\n                            \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         $+\\,\\text{ }C$" :question/worked-solution "Since $\\sqrt[5]{x}={x}^{1/5}$, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/5+1}}{(\\frac{1}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6/5}}{(\\frac{6}{5})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{6/5}}{6}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet's check our answer by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{6/5}}{6}+C) & = \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{6/5}}{6})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{6}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{6/5})+0 & = \\\\ \\frac{5}{6}\\cdot \\frac{6}{5}{x}^{6/5-1} & = \\\\ {x}^{1/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Radical Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064169 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064040 :question/id #uuid "c25e6037-3900-5314-b9a9-262fef07061c" :question/math-academy-id "e-368" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\dfrac 1 {x^3}$ and that $F'(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if\n\n$$\nF'(x) = f(x)\n$$\n\nthen integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF^{′}(x) &= f(x) \\\\\n\\intF^{′}(x)dx &= \\intf(x)dx \\\\\nF(x) &= \\intf(x)dx\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac 1 {x^3}= x^{-3}\n$$\n\nSo, we can use the power rule with $n=-3$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(x) &= \\intf(x)dx \\\\\n&= \\int\\frac{1}{x^{3}}dx \\\\\n&= \\intx^{-3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{x^{-3 + 1}}{-3 + 1} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{x^{-2}}{2} + C \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2x^{2}} + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3174cae9-484e-5ca3-8e5c-3c9cddc86145" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064722 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6a907ad-e7e6-5e6b-abb5-c41f16606605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{2/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062390} {:answer/id #uuid "dc6a8d1e-0787-5cc4-88df-ddf958e1c1d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x^{-1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062391} {:answer/id #uuid "16cba4e2-5699-54d0-b0af-01f1431acd0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}x^{5/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062392} {:answer/id #uuid "1b2e4389-0b1c-5925-9f9f-a24ca4b82e65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x^{1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062393} {:answer/id #uuid "70c4a8d8-2ed6-56b1-a746-7e1fc22b8346" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}x^{-1/3} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062394}] :answer-field/id #uuid "29757ce8-69c0-518a-9094-1478bb25152b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062389}] :question/id #uuid "35560944-ec26-532a-8ab4-c27135900127" :question/math-academy-id "q-29987" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = x^{-2/3}$ and that $F^{′}(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064723 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af3857a5-22ad-5617-8dd5-fe36c075509e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{5}x^{3/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062396} {:answer/id #uuid "dc2aaad4-968f-574b-842f-23871805d75b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062397} {:answer/id #uuid "35a1e4d4-ceef-5bb3-8381-e67a3cd0b1b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}x^{5/2} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062398} {:answer/id #uuid "40c5bb75-6c13-5d38-b5c4-d450f209706c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062399} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb175d1-16eb-5478-ba97-5cb4d5899d6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}x^{2/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062400}] :answer-field/id #uuid "4af9582e-4d65-5832-94c1-0ccba896c739" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062395}] :question/id #uuid "4f854a01-0859-5bcc-add9-c9a801f5da45" :question/math-academy-id "q-29989" :question/problem "Given that $f(x) = \\frac{1}{x^{3/5}}$ and that $F^{′}(x) = f(x)$, calculate $F(x)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233179 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25edeff2-faa4-50c4-bbfd-3291d7ac7694" :question/math-academy-id "q-113705" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4/3}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4/3}}={x}^{-4/3}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-4/3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4/3+1}}{(-\\frac{4}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/3}}{(-\\frac{1}{3})}+C \\\\  & =-3{x}^{-1/3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{{x}^{1/3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233751 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a192223-274d-5d58-847a-c92d2faa98df" :question/math-academy-id "q-29633" :question/problem "What is the antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}?$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}={x}^{-4}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-4$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{4}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-4+1}}{-4+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-3}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3{x}^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186233752 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8dcd24a2-ce5f-5ab6-8a92-814e8f1355a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-29662" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}$" :question/worked-solution "Note that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5/2}}={x}^{-5/2}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{5}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{5}}} & =\\int {x}^{-5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-5/2+1}}{-\\frac{5}{2}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}{x}^{-3/2}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3{x}^{3/2}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234299 :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "44529618-fcf7-5581-8bd3-a0df68de242f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71100" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/7}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{7}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/7+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{7}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{6/7}}{(\\frac{6}{7})}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{6}{x}^{6/7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Antiderivative of a Reciprocal Function"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064245 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064099 :question/id #uuid "60a223c7-3d1c-50d6-be7c-330ba039635c" :question/math-academy-id "e-491" :question/problem "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int uv' \\, \\textrm{d}x= uv - \\int vu' \\, \\textrm{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\displaystyle  \\int xe^{7x} \\textrm{d}x$ as $\\displaystyle  \\int uv'\\,\\textrm{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{7x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}-\\int \\frac{1}{7}{e}^{7x}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}\\int {e}^{7x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{7}(\\frac{{e}^{7x}}{7})+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}x{e}^{7x}-\\frac{1}{49}{e}^{7x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abe88143-989a-5967-bb08-16804e31d948" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050101 :topic/math-academy-id 1112 :topic/title "Integrating Exponential Functions Using Linear Substitution"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40e31ec9-8fca-5231-8200-ca80bc72b044" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{3}+\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272940} {:answer/id #uuid "997e80aa-81e0-539a-a4da-c477e354e208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273716} {:answer/id #uuid "c854fd56-2342-58ef-b090-fd79a6ccd523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274128} {:answer/id #uuid "df814db1-8188-5e1b-812c-d9b512f99e8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274359} {:answer/id #uuid "f0053e13-ea2e-5ba8-b9dc-186d83b1f4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{4x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274512}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "997e80aa-81e0-539a-a4da-c477e354e208" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273716} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a3e16d2-70ea-5fbe-9bd1-a83494641d8a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274842}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d59fc11b-e64a-50a7-ad7d-a5192fdda084" :question/math-academy-id "q-14434" :question/problem "$\\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{4x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}-\\int \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{4x}\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3}{2}x{e}^{4x}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{4x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{4x}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{4x}}{8}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064634 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a175a8cb-a6ee-5116-a42e-7718588e0c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(\\frac{1}{x} - \\frac{x}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061862} {:answer/id #uuid "b04d4f7a-8a20-52a1-b476-c32936814c77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x - 1) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061863} {:answer/id #uuid "da1a54a0-de58-5994-a0ad-8678d8dee9ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(1 - \\frac{x}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061864} {:answer/id #uuid "ec8d992b-235f-5112-bb41-ee409c14309a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x + \\frac{1}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061865} {:answer/id #uuid "638dab82-2814-5689-94e7-12a7d4a7dbd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2^{x}}{\\ln 2}(x - \\frac{1}{\\ln 2}) + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061866}] :answer-field/id #uuid "a6953c52-54a9-56b3-9aa6-e38c3e7044c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061861}] :question/id #uuid "faff3077-5b5e-5000-bc89-036983a07d8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-2425" :question/problem "Calculate $\\intx2^{x}dx$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250223 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26da406a-b1ee-533c-8e84-f3f3308fd3a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{2}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247767} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} {:answer/id #uuid "b96beb80-9254-5797-a25b-3e85eaa45af7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{3{e}^{-3x}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249082} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8237c1-5f1b-5b27-84a1-36bf62527629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{e}^{-3x}+\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249105} {:answer/id #uuid "f1f75f10-d4ff-5f2b-8f08-23ed364814bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249547}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6c223c6-0129-5a77-a5c1-dbc22604a28d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249062} :answer-field/id #uuid "16ddb17e-a21a-5bc8-bdfe-e5654290dd4d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249710}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a75c4b14-7006-556e-bd1e-e4613f35b446" :question/math-academy-id "q-114287" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=6x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=6 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe, substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 6x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =6x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 6\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 6x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2x{e}^{-3x}+2\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2x{e}^{-3x}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250224 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f62ef64-e190-59a0-80de-2a8c873c7f56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247983} {:answer/id #uuid "81cbaf36-0102-5b7f-97ff-d66d8054c9ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{4}+\\frac{5{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248574} {:answer/id #uuid "99e7a715-8634-5d28-bb4e-237d83c69b86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{8}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248798} {:answer/id #uuid "afef77b3-81af-530d-a6f6-eb398f03a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249004} {:answer/id #uuid "e249a080-5cfd-59dd-bdec-1e4e038339ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{8x}}{8}+\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{12}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afef77b3-81af-530d-a6f6-eb398f03a3c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249004} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a43b96e-f2d9-52db-aaf6-60b9ffaaf8e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249713}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "03919aa8-efb9-58ab-8664-d380cf005c1c" :question/math-academy-id "q-114288" :question/problem "$\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=4x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=4 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{8x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 4x\\cdot {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =4x\\cdot \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}-\\int \\frac{1}{8}{e}^{8x}\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 4x{e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}x{e}^{8x}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{e}^{8x}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{8x}}{16}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250225 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "022d7b7b-070a-51f5-bd49-94b4db34c49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(2x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247437} {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} {:answer/id #uuid "76108c8b-8f42-5f4a-9dd2-e847f09e6e05" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{x}{2})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248463} {:answer/id #uuid "8bfdc77f-bbbe-57f4-9329-f07738aa11a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248678} {:answer/id #uuid "c6440ae3-1132-5195-b3a2-356c7752e48e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e34cf00-1e95-5551-a888-a986e9043bfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247834} :answer-field/id #uuid "eede1f3b-85f2-5008-b473-3fcd59ae080b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250086}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "872e80da-db87-5cbe-89ef-83c58a2b3950" :question/math-academy-id "q-114289" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{3}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′} & ={3}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{3}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\int \\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-\\frac{{3}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{3}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04df1fbb-68fc-5df3-a2f3-5de5f64fbd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247459} {:answer/id #uuid "059681dd-6855-5de5-adb1-fa9432d5314c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{3}-6){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247472} {:answer/id #uuid "19b553b9-fab9-540b-be56-77f1ce0d0a8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247659} {:answer/id #uuid "c43e1a7b-f3a2-5b76-a623-7db7da101361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249166} {:answer/id #uuid "ec744b0d-6761-589d-ad26-06e817b26961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{x}{2}-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04df1fbb-68fc-5df3-a2f3-5de5f64fbd4f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247459} :answer-field/id #uuid "f3af4228-49fc-5b51-b5a2-20758a8a7ffa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250099}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "623d728c-8114-50ed-8705-4853f0ddb4f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-114290" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x-2\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{x+3}\\, & ⟹\\,v={e}^{x+3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x-2)\\cdot {e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x-2)\\cdot {e}^{x+3}-\\int {e}^{x+3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x-2){e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x-2){e}^{x+3}-\\int {e}^{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(x-2){e}^{x+3}-{e}^{x+3}+C \\\\  & =(x-3){e}^{x+3}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186250227 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36a625e0-f342-5d88-863b-2cc610f12c52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2x-1){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247918} {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} {:answer/id #uuid "4d558edc-f058-5d64-aa0f-acff177c0e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2-3x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248117} {:answer/id #uuid "7aa27907-71bc-5690-9d5a-5ea98a3a03cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2x-1){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186248503} {:answer/id #uuid "cd15176c-1580-5959-a4f3-0332eefaf817" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(2-x){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186249245}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e06e8db-4185-544e-9ae5-0b2a2e9f7015" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186247972} :answer-field/id #uuid "f37b9f98-70f3-5724-8992-60b01c3a21f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250097}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1022e01f-7a5a-562e-a877-5ba5b3c9edd4" :question/math-academy-id "q-114293" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x-4\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x-4)\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x-4)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x-4){e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-4){e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x-3){e}^{-3x}}{3}+C \\\\  & =(1-x){e}^{-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259696 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "271f180d-3faa-5476-a054-bf22f99176bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-2{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257122} {:answer/id #uuid "4d6abd70-33c0-5278-82e7-159c499aad7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}+{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257447} {:answer/id #uuid "9ef47045-065b-557c-a1cb-f734f625b80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258180} {:answer/id #uuid "b34f8ff6-8e7b-5a4a-b1de-16e75dced547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{e}^{-x}-3x{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258342} {:answer/id #uuid "d29bd4f3-02bb-5eb5-b6ba-5b257eab8b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-x}-x{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ef47045-065b-557c-a1cb-f734f625b80c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258180} :answer-field/id #uuid "47fd06f4-4187-5190-9ee6-b13410e9fa3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259160}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1a4ea9ed-1853-52ed-ab6f-46794d76e304" :question/math-academy-id "q-12462" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-{e}^{-x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot (-{e}^{-x})-\\int (-{e}^{-x})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-3x{e}^{-x}+3\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-3x{e}^{-x}-3{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} {:answer/id #uuid "394ffebc-fc15-59d2-b922-cf67e8668a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257288} {:answer/id #uuid "98f26b34-1c20-50e4-ae9f-0696b345d0e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258130} {:answer/id #uuid "dee11791-9fa1-5f13-86b4-6751c7ac156e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{3x}}{3}+\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258723} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7bf65f-10a0-5fb7-85b0-318f615112d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{9}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30b012af-7da3-57e7-b3fe-ad695b25321d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257210} :answer-field/id #uuid "4626c1aa-c3c9-5543-a9d9-8d0984251445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259158}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d57f8c60-94ea-5515-8561-35af7ac97700" :question/math-academy-id "q-12556" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{3})\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{-3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{x{e}^{-3x}}{3}-\\frac{{e}^{-3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259830 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "236b60cf-ff8d-5674-870b-bcaaf8d37985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{5x}}{5}+\\frac{3x{e}^{5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257078} {:answer/id #uuid "4d557db5-ba1a-5b05-b356-74912875cd91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}+\\frac{3x{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257446} {:answer/id #uuid "5e1550eb-3fe9-5df7-a495-0e900c02c6de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{25}-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257606} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe0799-f21d-5fea-a233-c69798ab78fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257623} {:answer/id #uuid "92ec0b8f-683f-538a-921f-014ccb202f1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x{e}^{-5x}}{25}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ffe0799-f21d-5fea-a233-c69798ab78fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257623} :answer-field/id #uuid "793c5074-4fab-55cd-94b8-d8144c552545" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259236}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a269e9e4-ba48-5393-8b91-051e5b1bc073" :question/math-academy-id "q-12559" :question/problem "Calculate $\\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x+5\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{-5x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (3x+5)\\cdot {e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(3x+5)\\cdot (-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5})-\\int (-\\frac{{e}^{-5x}}{5})\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3x+5){e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}+\\frac{3}{5}\\int {e}^{-5x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{(3x+5){e}^{-5x}}{5}-\\frac{3{e}^{-5x}}{25}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259831 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "109d035c-6ffc-56c3-8581-53bca2233532" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256935} {:answer/id #uuid "209845fa-bfdf-5169-8a21-91e5d6fa04ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257046} {:answer/id #uuid "5be69881-f41a-506d-a346-ccfa892bacb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}-\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257582} {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} {:answer/id #uuid "a0da683e-5345-5b81-9094-abd5ff0ec151" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186258191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a4a072e-05a9-58e4-83e0-911e978158f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257721} :answer-field/id #uuid "b284ab05-c542-58e4-99b1-8ce31da489d2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259344}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b258b659-45f7-5842-b37a-ee530a2eb1b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-12560" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x+7\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (x+7)\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =(x+7)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (x+7){e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+7){e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186290531 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c795865-da64-5e14-9024-3c7c02d718c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(\\frac{1}{x}-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288124} {:answer/id #uuid "51fe0db3-d702-5875-904d-f79bd58f19bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-1)+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288600} {:answer/id #uuid "6e5a066a-1db0-5b07-b438-285b415f19bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288802} {:answer/id #uuid "9611c013-b6fd-5217-9d39-883aca3329d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(1-\\frac{x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289037} {:answer/id #uuid "c91e7928-ce32-56f4-8b9f-43257961903a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186289366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e5a066a-1db0-5b07-b438-285b415f19bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186288802} :answer-field/id #uuid "94c0f155-a00b-507b-a0ba-cb1120435b6e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00c040ca-17ee-59e4-9387-a983daa9bae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-2420" :question/problem "$\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int x{5}^{x}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=1 \\\\ {v}^{′}={5}^{x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot {5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x{5}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\int \\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{x{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)}-\\frac{{5}^{x}}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5))^{2}}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{5}^{x}}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}(x-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5})+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fea6d91-968c-5f4d-8499-0425dc5d7fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(3x+2){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362862} {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} {:answer/id #uuid "f721fccd-de41-549f-b75e-093592b0c032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+4){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362864} {:answer/id #uuid "7db9ef7b-e876-5195-b2bc-5e90b186c364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-3){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362865} {:answer/id #uuid "cab8da55-0308-5e36-8634-1b58557947b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(4x-1){e}^{3x}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df58de38-7310-5f19-9844-03c75ef49b7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362863} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bcef777-2395-5b4a-81aa-40676383c492" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bd0da194-e627-59a2-b874-56e9ce11e475" :question/math-academy-id "q-114291" :question/problem "Calculate the integral $\\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x.$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2x+1\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=2 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{3x}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (2x+1)\\cdot {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =(2x+1)\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{3x}}{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (2x+1){e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{3x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(2x+1){e}^{3x}}{3}-\\frac{2{e}^{3x}}{9}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x+1){e}^{3x}}{9}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362996 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ba8cff6-a436-587b-947b-b845d40cdf1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362998} {:answer/id #uuid "0bf7139d-5b6a-513e-8c05-ea38b19064dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362999} {:answer/id #uuid "1a22e02f-c34e-55ad-b5ee-acd29d97566a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363000} {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a00544-29af-5a0e-9dbd-8c18e64ae108" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}+\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363002}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3c30e70-a737-5f41-9c71-a8d0f2188c7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363001} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4e46148-8029-5a37-a794-c93ccb0b0139" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362997}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "708f4971-ac44-5610-9dca-92afa6cd2300" :question/math-academy-id "q-12558" :question/problem "$\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "To solve this integral, we use the by-parts formula, given by\n\n$$\n\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x=uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe need to express $\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\text{d}x$ as $\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Therefore, we set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=3x\\, & ⟹\\,{u}^{′}=3 \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{2x+5}\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute the above into the integration by parts formula, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int 3x\\cdot {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =3x\\cdot \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\int \\frac{{e}^{2x+5}}{2}\\cdot 3\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3x{e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{2x+5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3x{e}^{2x+5}}{2}-\\frac{3{e}^{2x+5}}{4}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Using Integration by Parts to Compute an Indefinite Integral Containing an Exponential Expression"}]}
